Subject: [#94-10-402] Tides and the Biosphere

Harvey Newstrom wrote:

> A recent issue of _Skeptical Inquirer_ (the most recent, I think) had a good
> article discussing why the tidal pull of the moon (let alone the stars) is
> too small to have any significant effect on us.

  Maybe on us directly, but surely not on the biosphere.  Tidal sloshing,
induced by both sun and moon, is a strong shaper of bays and estuaries, and
a strong mixer and distributer of nutrient in some of the most productive
(biologically) areas of the world.

